{
	"info": {
		"name": "Filinq batch anonymisation output folder layout",
		"description": "anonymisation-batch-output-folder-layout task 11. Three text files in one folder go through a folder batch: extract, anonymise (format kept). The anonymised copies land in the folder's anonymised/ subfolder under their own names, and no _anonymized file is left beside the sources. It needs a live instance with entity detection, so it sits in tests/integration/live/, outside the flat glob the CI Newman job runs. Run it with: npx newman run tests/integration/live/anonymisation-output-layout.postman_collection.json --env-var baseUrl=$BASE_URL --env-var adminUser=$ADMIN_USER --env-var adminPass=$ADMIN_PASS. Before anonymising, a second account (created here, reviewerUser) checks each document in the review workbench and sets the redaction mark, because four eyes are required: whoever checked may not also anonymise",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
